                <pb facs="0607" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5727/61.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 129.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 8th instant, respecting the application to other countries
                    of the administrative changes in United States customs-houses, which derive from
                    the new German-American commercial agreement.</p>
                <p>While expressing my best thanks for this communication, I beg to inform you that
                    I immediately acquainted His Majesty’s Government with its contents.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Esme Howard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
